CHANGE LOG

2.0.0 (2026-JUN)

Major Performance & Modernization Release
This release brings a significant modernization of the extension to C++17 standards, with major focus on performance, reduced memory copies, and code quality.

* Key Improvements *

**Performance Gains:**
 - Insert operations ~12% faster
 - to_array() / iteration ~36% faster
 - Significant reduction in temporary std::string copies through widespread use of std::string_view

**C++17 Modernization:**
 - Full migration to std::string_view for all lookup operations (read, exists, remove)
 - Added const correctness and noexcept where appropriate
 - Modernized class design with deleted copy constructor, default move semantics, and in-class initializers
 - Cleaner iterator implementation with proper Zend handler signatures

**Code Quality & Stability:**
 - Replaced legacy macros with modern inline fetch helpers (php_sparsehashmap_fetch_object)
 - Fixed multiple bugs in iterator, clone, and object handlers
 - Improved memory reporting and garbage collection behavior
 - Better null safety and error handling

**Build & Compatibility:**
 - Updated config.m4 for C++17 requirement
 - Cleaner header structure and include guards
 - Improved compatibility with PHP 8.4+


* Benchmark Results (900,000 items) *

 - Insert: 5.09s → 4.48s
 - to_array(): 0.174s → 0.111s
 - Memory usage remains highly efficient (SparseHashMap core unchanged)

* Breaking Changes *

 - Minimum requirement is now C++17 and PHP 8.1+

***Internal***

 - Extensive refactoring of object handlers, iterator, and core C++ wrapper
 - Removed redundant string conversions and legacy code patterns
 - Much improved maintainability and standards compliance

1.0.3 - PHP 8.4 update
* The zend_object_iterator_funcs valid member has changed its signature from
  int(*)(zend_object_iterator *) to zend_result(*)(zend_object_iterator *) to
  be more in line with what callbacks are returning.